  "record": {
    "read_status": "full",
    "file_problem": "none",
    "relation": "cites_only",
    "tranche": "T6",
    "tranche_reason": "The study cites induction-head work in related literature but does not measure induction heads, their formation, or their causal role. Its experiments evaluate task performance on synthetic ICL benchmarks, not the specific behaviours named in the claim versions.",
    "gate_note": "The paper states that induction heads correlate with ICL and that MQAR is related to associative recall, but those are citations or framing. Its own experiments do not identify, intervene on, or measure induction heads, token-index loss changes, or head-level mechanisms. The synthetic-language ICL results are recorded under fits_no_version because they concern ICL performance but do not measure the mechanisms or specific ICL behaviours named by the versions.",
    "test_reason": "The study trains Transformers, Mamba, S4 and hybrids from scratch on synthetic ICL tasks and reports task loss or accuracy only. It never identifies, ablates or tracks induction heads or previous-token heads. It does not measure formation timing, loss bumps or per-token-index loss in pretrained language models. Olsson et al. is cited only in related work and to motivate MQAR.",
    "authors_conclusion": "Mostly correct. The authors conclude that Mamba can perform ICL comparably to Transformers on many tasks and beats them on sparse parity, but fails at vector-valued associative recall. The hybrid MambaFormer, with an initial Mamba block and no positional encoding, performs well on all tasks. They draw no conclusions about induction heads.",
    "recipe": "none",
    "recipe_differences": "The study trains models from scratch on synthetic task distributions and evaluates task performance; it does not reproduce induction-head measurements or the original training-loss and token-index analysis.",
    "method_sensitivity": "The study reports task and architecture differences; it also notes sensitivity to learning rate and optimizer choices in its experiments, but does not test their effect on induction-head formation.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "On vector MQAR (Table 3), Mamba's test MSE is 0.15–0.86. Transformers reach about 1e-4 to 1e-7, and MambaFormer about 1e-5 to 1e-7. Adding one attention block to Mamba largely closes the gap.",
        "proposed_claim": "Attention-free SSMs (Mamba) perform associative recall, a generalisation of the induction task, much worse than attention-based or hybrid models at small scale.",
        "row_ids": []
      },
      {
        "finding": "Architecture differences on the GINC and RegBench synthetic-language ICL benchmarks (Tables 4–5).",
        "proposed_claim": "Synthetic-language ICL performance varies by architecture and training length; hybrids score highest on RegBench.",
